| `scripts/exit_code_table.py` | Fails when the exit-code table in the limits guide differs from the `ExitCode` enum and from what each script `make verify` runs can return, and writes it without `--check`; with `--shell` it does the same for the shell helper `scripts/exit_codes.sh`. | `make check-exit-codes` | [`scripts/exit_code_table.py --check`](settings.md#command-line-flags) | Does not hold exits to the helper: `tests/integration/test_exit_gate.py` does. Does not write the hand-written table below the generated region. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
